<title>MALAYSIA: Kiara Emas debuts at 8.90 rgt.</title>
<headline>Kiara Emas debuts at 8.90 rgt.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian coachbuilder Kiara Emas Asia Industries Bhd debuted on the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange on Thursday at 8.90 ringgit against an offer price of 3.00 ringgit per share.</p>
<p>The company had offered six million shares for sale.  </p>
<p>Kiara Emas is listed on the small-capitalised Second Board of the exchange.</p>
<p>The company is principally involved in the manufacture, fabrication and assembly of body parts for coaches, buses and trucks.</p>
<p>Mayban Securities estimated its net profit for the year ending March 31 1997 to be 9.1 million ringgit, compared to 7.4 million ringgit in the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>Mayban gave fair valuation of the stock at 8.70 ringgit.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
</text>
